		<label>Type 69 RPG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 85mm PG-7. 1-round tube. Single-Shot.
		
The Type 69 rocket-propelled grenade launcher is a Chinese copy of the Soviet RPG-7, reverse engineered in the 1960s out of a need for improved anti-armor weapons during the Sino-Soviet border conflict. A highly effective and cheap weapon, the Type 69 formed the backbone of PLA man-portable anti-tank armaments for three decades after its introduction, only being supplemented by newer systems like the PF-98 in the late 1990s. The Type 69 is still in PLA service in some capacity, and is also still produced for export abroad.</description>
